\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Post-training gain}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{post-training}

\p{Let #{\pi_0} be the base policy and let #{\Pi_P} be the random policy
returned by post-training protocol #{P}. The \strong{post-training gain} is}

##{
  \Delta_{\mathrm{ev}}(P;D,b)
  =\mathbb E\left[J_{\mathcal Q_{\mathrm{ev}}}(\Pi_P;D,b)\right]
   -J_{\mathcal Q_{\mathrm{ev}}}(\pi_0;D,b).
}

\p{Section 3.5 of \citef{sutton2018reinforcement} defines expected policy
performance. FTIP takes its difference before and after a random post-training
procedure. The outer expectation covers the training data and rollouts. It
also covers environment and optimizer randomness.}

\p{The comparison uses the same evaluator #{D} and budget #{b} for both
policies. A positive value reports a measured capability change. It does not
by itself distinguish elicitation, acquisition, leakage, or reward hacking.}
